{
  "source": "Prompts/critical-thinking-1.mp4",
  "duration": 190.589375,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.16,
      "text": "Knowledge is the foundation, but how you use it determines the outcome."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.84,
      "end": 8.26,
      "text": "Critical thinking is the active process of questioning what you hear,"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.78,
      "end": 11.96,
      "text": "examining the evidence and deciding whether a claim holds up."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.6,
      "end": 14.68,
      "text": "This infographic shows how the pieces fit."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.46,
      "end": 18.88,
      "text": "On the left, knowledge represents facts, acting as an alarm system."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.78,
      "end": 24.42,
      "text": "On the right, critical thinking actively questions claims and considers other explanations."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.5,
      "end": 27.76,
      "text": "Combining them leads to better questions and decisions."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.76,
      "end": 32.32,
      "text": "Being smarter than the tool means habitually asking what must be true."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.16,
      "end": 37.52,
      "text": "In 2015, headlines around the world announced that eating chocolate helps you lose weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.24,
      "end": 41.02,
      "text": "One front page even ran the headline, slim by chocolate."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.78,
      "end": 43.4,
      "text": "That headline likely made you pause."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.16,
      "end": 46.78,
      "text": "That moment of hesitation is critical thinking starting up."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.42,
      "end": 51.04,
      "text": "The immediate next step is to ask whether the evidence actually supports the claim."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.82,
      "end": 55.26,
      "text": "When readers evaluate a headline like this, they usually fall into two categories."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.11,
      "end": 61.14,
      "text": "Both groups hear the exact same claim, but they apply very different levels of scrutiny."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.1,
      "end": 64.68,
      "text": "The first reaction is taking the claim at face value."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.48,
      "end": 70.72,
      "text": "A reader hears the claim, thinks it sounds appealing, and chooses to believe it without any internal friction."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.78,
      "end": 77.24,
      "text": "The critical thinking approach involves stopping to ask what is actually behind the claim before accepting it."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.82,
      "end": 81.4,
      "text": "You must force yourself to pause and activate this skeptical approach"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.4,
      "end": 84.56,
      "text": "whenever a claim sounds exactly like something you want to believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.32,
      "end": 90.76,
      "text": "While the chocolate study actually took place, the researchers designed it from the beginning to be flimsy."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.62,
      "end": 93.3,
      "text": "The methodology illustrates the problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.14,
      "end": 99.66,
      "text": "The researchers used only 15 participants, yet they measured 18 different variables about them."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.42,
      "end": 102.92,
      "text": "When you take that many measurements on such a small group,"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.34,
      "end": 107.4,
      "text": "random chance guarantees that at least one result will falsely look like a discovery."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.18,
      "end": 110.06,
      "text": "In this case, the data was just noise."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.06,
      "end": 115.88,
      "text": "Furthermore, the research institute cited in the study was nothing more than a basic website."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.74,
      "end": 119.0,
      "text": "The author was a journalist running a sting operation."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.96,
      "end": 126.78,
      "text": "He wanted to prove that a terrible study with a clickable headline would be shared globally before anyone bothered to verify the facts."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.62,
      "end": 127.9,
      "text": "It worked."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.06,
      "end": 133.98,
      "text": "Critical thinking requires the ability to read between the lines and verify the authority of a source,"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.5,
      "end": 136.36,
      "text": "especially when the claim is highly appealing."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.36,
      "end": 140.7,
      "text": "You can sharpen your critical thinking by building five specific habits."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.54,
      "end": 143.5,
      "text": "Each habit is a question you ask yourself."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.22,
      "end": 144.84,
      "text": "Habit one."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.52,
      "end": 146.44,
      "text": "Is it actually right?"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.1,
      "end": 147.66,
      "text": "Check the evidence."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.5,
      "end": 149.16,
      "text": "Habit two."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.84,
      "end": 150.46,
      "text": "Do I know enough?"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.16,
      "end": 152.42,
      "text": "Recognize your knowledge limits."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.2,
      "end": 153.78,
      "text": "Habit three."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.56,
      "end": 154.82,
      "text": "What's missing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 155.82,
      "end": 156.86,
      "text": "Seek alternative explanations."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.2,
      "end": 158.66,
      "text": "Habit four."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.3,
      "end": 160.04,
      "text": "Why am I convinced?"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.74,
      "end": 162.84,
      "text": "Is it evidence or a desire to believe?"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.48,
      "end": 164.92,
      "text": "Finally, habit five."
    },
    {
      "start": 165.78,
      "end": 166.32,
      "text": "What's my call?"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.96,
      "end": 167.92,
      "text": "Decide what to believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.78,
      "end": 172.0,
      "text": "These five questions are essential tools when interacting with AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 172.98,
      "end": 178.88,
      "text": "AI can help you sign a flaw in your thinking, or it can confidently repeat a mistake back to you."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.48,
      "end": 181.78,
      "text": "You are responsible for judging which is happening."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.58,
      "end": 184.66,
      "text": "AI amplifies whatever you bring to it."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.22,
      "end": 186.94,
      "text": "Good thinking in, sharper output."
    }
  ],
